  <section>
    <h2>Woolwich Dispensary Overview</h2>
    <p>Woolwich is a small Sagadahoc County town along US-1 across the Kennebec River from Bath. The town's adult-use retail market is concentrated along the Route 1 corridor and serves a broad mid-coast catchment including Woolwich, Bath, Wiscasset, and parts of Brunswick. Five storefronts operate in Woolwich, with a mix of medical-focused and adult-use operators. The Woolwich retail cluster is convenient for mid-coast residents who don't want to drive to the Brunswick or Bath clusters. Pricing tracks the state median for mid-coast.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dispensaries in Woolwich</h2>
    <p>The table below lists the licensed adult-use storefronts currently operating in Woolwich. Hours, menus, and pricing change frequently — always verify directly with the operator before making the trip.</p>
    <table aria-label="Licensed dispensaries in Woolwich, Maine">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Operator</th><th scope="col">Address</th><th scope="col">Website</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <tr><td>LANDRACE CANNABIS</td><td>97 Main St</td><td><a href="https://www.landracecanna.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.landracecanna.com</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>HIGHLY CANNACO RETAIL #5, LLC</td><td>73 Main St</td><td>(not listed)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>All storefronts are licensed by the Maine Office of Cannabis Policy (OCP) for both adult-use and medical sales. Medical patients pay only the 5.5% state sales tax; adult-use customers pay the 10% state excise on top of the 5.5% sales tax, for a combined 15.5% effective rate.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What to Expect on a First Visit</h2>
    <p>If you are 21 or older with a valid government-issued photo ID (Maine driver's license, out-of-state ID, or passport), you can walk into any adult-use dispensary in Woolwich and purchase. The process is the same as a liquor store: show ID at the door, browse the menu, place an order, pay. Most stores accept cash and debit; many have an on-site ATM and some offer cashless debit through a third-party processor (there is typically a $2-3 fee).</p>
    <p>First-time visitors should expect a brief intake — the <a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-staffing-licensing">budtender</a> will ask if you have used cannabis before, what effects you are looking for, and whether you have any preferences on format (flower, edible, vape, concentrate). Be honest; the staff is trained to recommend the right product for the right goal. There is no medical exam and no requirement to disclose your reasons for using.</p>
    <p>For medical patients, bring your Maine medical cannabis card (or a valid out-of-state card if your state has a reciprocity agreement with Maine). Medical patients have access to higher-dose products, lower taxes, and the MMJP-only dispensaries that do not appear on the adult-use retail map.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Pricing in Woolwich</h2>
    <p>Pricing at Woolwich dispensaries tracks the Sagadahoc County, with the usual seasonal and competitive variation. As of mid-2026:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Flower (eighth, 3.5g):</strong> $35-50, premium indoor can run higher</li>
      <li><strong>Pre-rolls (single 1g):</strong> $12-18, multi-packs $25-50</li>
      <li><strong>Edibles (100mg THC pack):</strong> $20-35, depending on format and brand</li>
      <li><strong>Distillate cartridges (1g):</strong> $35-50</li>
      <li><strong>Concentrates (1g):</strong> $40-80, depending on quality and format</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Medical patients save the 10% state excise — a meaningful discount on larger purchases. Adult-use customers should ask about first-time buyer promotions, birthday discounts, and weekday specials, which most Woolwich stores offer.</p>
  </section>

